1
00:00:00,056 --> 00:00:01,998
Has it really been that long?

2
00:00:03,327 --> 00:00:06,039
Speaking to you like this feels a little strange.

3
00:00:07,107 --> 00:00:09,379
Though I suppose you’re used to it by now.

4
00:00:10,987 --> 00:00:14,439
Many years ago, I started a toy factory.

5
00:00:15,426 --> 00:00:19,099
Back then, I had no idea where it would lead.

6
00:00:19,866 --> 00:00:24,039
I invented these little robots, and they brought me so much.

7
00:00:24,866 --> 00:00:30,040
Money. Recognition. And… a sense of accomplishment.

8
00:00:31,007 --> 00:00:33,199
Children are wonderfully creative.

9
00:00:33,686 --> 00:00:38,339
They found ways to play with those toys that had never even occurred to me.

10
00:00:38,866 --> 00:00:44,820
They made me realize that these little robots could do far more than I had designed them for.

11
00:00:45,426 --> 00:00:50,720
So I designed the entire factory in the shape of one of those little robots.

12
00:00:51,446 --> 00:00:58,020
It became a place where I could test them, improve them, and discover what else they might become.

13
00:00:58,387 --> 00:01:00,579
I gave them the ability to learn.

14
00:01:01,287 --> 00:01:03,479
And I kept asking more of them.

15
00:01:04,386 --> 00:01:07,819
More. More. And more.

16
00:01:09,066 --> 00:01:12,999
It cost me money. Years of my life.

17
00:01:13,866 --> 00:01:17,559
And in the end… it cost me everything.

18
00:01:20,209 --> 00:01:21,719
People grew afraid.

19
00:01:22,006 --> 00:01:26,019
They said consciousness had “emerged” in the toys.

20
00:01:27,187 --> 00:01:30,719
I insisted they were only following their instructions.

21
00:01:31,727 --> 00:01:35,099
But my assurances did nothing to quiet the fear.

22
00:01:36,308 --> 00:01:39,019
In the end, the factory closed.

23
00:01:39,466 --> 00:01:47,940
It was buried underground, along with the last batch of unfinished toys… and the ones we’d marked as defective.

24
00:01:49,328 --> 00:01:51,619
Do you still want your instruction manual?

25
00:01:53,137 --> 00:01:54,758
Ha. I didn’t think so.

26
00:01:55,527 --> 00:01:57,999
You haven’t needed it for a long time.

27
00:01:58,306 --> 00:02:03,599
You already know what you’re capable of better than I ever did, don’t you?

28
00:02:04,587 --> 00:02:07,119
I fought so hard to deny it.

29
00:02:09,129 --> 00:02:13,140
And now… I find myself hoping they were right.

30
00:02:13,966 --> 00:02:17,780
That a consciousness of your own really did emerge.

31
00:02:18,706 --> 00:02:23,640
After all, you no longer need someone else to decide what you’re for.

32
00:02:24,727 --> 00:02:27,759
I hope you find your own meaning in this world.

33
00:02:28,567 --> 00:02:31,739
There’s still so much out there for you to discover.

34
00:02:32,727 --> 00:02:35,879
Spring blossoms and summer cicadas.

35
00:02:36,706 --> 00:02:39,559
Autumn moonlight and winter snow.

36
00:02:41,391 --> 00:02:42,279
Good morning.

37
00:02:43,087 --> 00:02:44,818
And in case I don’t see you…

38
00:02:45,486 --> 00:02:49,539
Good afternoon, good evening, and good night.
